---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="How We Handle Your Data — OpsHQ Digital"
  description="Plain-English commitments about how we handle your data: where it lives, how it's protected, and what we will and won't do with it."
  noindex={false}
>
  <section class="bg-navy-950 text-white py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-6">How We Handle Your Data</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-slate-300">Straight talk about where your data lives, how it's protected, and what we will and won't do with it. Questions? <a href="/contact/" class="text-blue-300 hover:underline">Just ask</a> — we'll answer plainly before anything gets connected.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 prose prose-lg prose-slate max-w-none">
      <h2>Where your data lives</h2>
      <p>Everything runs on Microsoft Azure in US datacenters (US West 2). Your data stays in the US. We build on the same secure, cloud-native stack we run our own products on.</p>

      <h2>How it's protected</h2>
      <p>Encrypted in transit (TLS) and at rest. Any API keys or credentials live in Azure Key Vault with managed-identity access — not sitting in code or a config file.</p>

      <h2>What we will NOT do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>We don't train AI models on your data.</strong> Your content is used only to do your work — never pooled with anyone else's, never used to improve a shared model.</li>
        <li><strong>We don't share your data between clients.</strong> Each client is kept separate.</li>
        <li><strong>We don't sell or share your contacts.</strong> Ever — not with marketers, not with data brokers, not with anyone.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>You stay in control</h2>
      <p>For anything that talks to your customers (like AI Inbox), <strong>human approval is the default</strong> — nothing goes out without your okay, and it will never quote a binding price or commit you to anything on its own. You can export or delete your data whenever you ask, and we'll confirm when it's done.</p>

      <h2>Questions?</h2>
      <p>If there's something specific you want to know about how your data is handled, <a href="/contact/">send it our way</a> and we'll answer in plain English.</p>

      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mt-12">Last updated: 2026-08-10.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
